  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Until this summer, Saint-Raphaël's supervised beaches were off-limits to dogs in the bathing season, even on a leash. For summer 2026, the town opened a "caniplage" on Beaurivage beach, next to the Diana jetty, right in the town centre; Nice-Matin (17 July 2026) describes it as accessible until 30 September (2026 season over).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Estérel Côte d'Azur confirms that Beau Rivage is among the beaches for dogs, while the supervised beaches and several other Saint-Raphaël sites remain off-limits to dogs in the bathing season. At the opening, it was announced that dogs had to stay on a leash, that category 1 and 2 dogs were excluded and that identification was required; these details could not be re-checked. The 2026 season ended on 30 September.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: to find out whether the arrangement will be renewed, call the town hall (04 94 82 15 00). In the meantime, Plage du Pacha in Fréjus, cited by Nice-Matin as an alternative, is a neighbouring dog beach.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Beau Rivage is a pebble beach, supervised in season (lifeguard post, until mid-September), lined by a tree-shaded park with a large car park, children's play area, minigolf and bandstand; toilets, showers and Handiplage in season (Estérel Côte d'Azur). The park and Saint-Raphaël town centre are steps away; the rules for dogs in the park are not specified by these sources. Outside the dog area, the supervised beach remains off-limits to dogs in the bathing season.</p>

    </div>

